 "notes": "All values are REAL published rates from the Indian Bullion & Jewellers Association (IBJA), India's national bullion benchmark. Convention: IBJA Fine Gold (999) AM fixing per gram and Silver (999) AM fixing per kg, excluding 3% GST and making charges. Sep 1-3 gold values use exact decimals from IBJA's official daily rate sheet (per-10g values divided by 10); all other days use the per-gram figures exactly as published by The Economic Times' daily IBJA reports (which round the per-10g fixing to whole rupees). Null days: Sep 5-6, 12-13, 19-20, 26-27 are Saturdays/Sundays on which IBJA publishes no rates; Sep 14 (Monday) is also null because IBJA published no rates that day - ET's Sep 14 article states IBJA was 'yet to update' and ET's Sep 15 article compares Sep 11 PM directly against Sep 15 AM. Nothing is invented or interpolated: each populated value was read from a published source on 2026-09-30. Note: the ET article URL for the Sep 11 rates carries a 'september-14' slug but its title and content are the September 11, 2026 report. Distinct retail/city series (ABP Live, Goodreturns, jeweller websites, Sunday Guardian's Delhi retail series) and All India Bullion's separate India-wide history were deliberately NOT mixed in."
